{
	chapter.05C3ACD631F0D447.title: "II: Mycolorology"
	chapter.7335A7B59A697BAD.title: "I: Hot Bricks In Your Area"
	chapter_group.0863DFE6E54CBB77.title: "Main Chapters"
	file.0000000000000001.title: "The Wild Red Yonder"
	quest.120084FAE00B31E2.quest_desc: ["Prove you've got a steady source of food up there, and we can send you some new crops!"]
	quest.120084FAE00B31E2.title: "Potato, Potahto"
	quest.163F099D955ED62E.quest_desc: ["This pack contains many guidebooks for all the various mods. Here's a convenient book to keep them all in!"]
	quest.194318B1AC72B873.quest_desc: ["Cooking sealed wood in this furnace will net you some charcoal and a tiny bit of creosote oil. Cooking that charcoal again will get you coal coke, and a lot more creosote! Coal coke is a very good fuel source for furnaces."]
	quest.194318B1AC72B873.quest_subtitle: "Bigger, bigger, yet bigger"
	quest.19D201B45F89D15E.quest_desc: ["By mixing together the starch from potatoes with water and sand and letting it set, you can make a primitive brick about as strong as concrete or stone! "]
	quest.19D201B45F89D15E.title: "Starcrete Bricks"
	quest.1F42046CD1963186.quest_desc: ["As a state of the art Mars colonization robot, you may think you are above needing to eat food. This would be an incorrect assumption! You are equipped with a bioreactor energy core, which requires you to provide it with a large variety of foods. Unlike some older models, however, you are not penalized for eating the same foods, but rather encouraged to experiment with culinary innovations to find foods that give you the best buffs."]
	quest.2438036AD88F69DB.quest_desc: ["Contrary to its name, the Ember Bore is a multiblock that can excavate many things, not just Ember! Put it on some snow blocks, route it into a melter, and you've got automated water!"]
	quest.2438036AD88F69DB.title: "Automated Water"
	quest.2498E75776A6FEA9.quest_subtitle: "Durable Wood"
	quest.38F52F65D4B01520.quest_desc: ["You can now grow crops! In space! Isn't that wild!?"]
	quest.38F52F65D4B01520.title: "Hydroponics!"
	quest.3C0CF14CB97704B9.quest_desc: ["You can fill up a bucket of water with the ice shards you've mined up, but it's not gonna be cheap...."]
	quest.3C0CF14CB97704B9.title: "Out of Water?"
	quest.3E19C7F1D0AD1C0E.quest_desc: ["Water freezes on the surface, so you'll need somewhere to store it all!"]
	quest.45B8E6237B2D3F93.quest_desc: [
		"The Ember Activator can turn crystal Ember into its energy form, Ember Flux. You can use this to power dwarven machinery!"
		""
		"&oTip: to route Ember flux to a machine, the Activator needs to have an Emitter on it. The recieving machine needs a Reciever. Then, right click the emitter with the hammer. It will clink and glow orange. You can then link it to the receptor by right clicking it. Emitters can be linked to only one receptor, and they won't send until they are powered by a redstone signal. This is the first rule of the Embers mod: If it doesn't work, slap a lever on it!&r"
	]
	quest.45B8E6237B2D3F93.quest_subtitle: "Fireball"
	quest.45B8E6237B2D3F93.title: "Ember Machinery"
	quest.50A946EE8DE8D308.quest_desc: ["Now you are able to get more metal per metal out of your ores, as well as shape them into various casts!"]
	quest.5376E05C4F4D4051.quest_desc: ["In your pursuit of better bricks, the small electric furnace you've scrounged together simply isn't hot enough!"]
	quest.5964B593F1CE00FC.quest_desc: ["You can salvage some mechanical components and scrap metal from the old radio we have lying around!"]
	quest.5E0AC2F5932C0F4D.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to Mars! Your mission is simple: turn this planet from a barren wasteland to something habitable by human life. We know you can do it! "
		"You may be wondering why you have nothing to your name but a couple crates of potatoes, miscellaneous cooking equipment, and a super expensive life sustaining biodome. Well, truth be told, we spent most of our money on the super expensive life sustaining biodome. And we're counting on you to make us our investment back!"
		"Everyone here at Q•Bit Ltd. is counting on you! Don't let us down!"
	]
	quest.5E0AC2F5932C0F4D.quest_subtitle: "What were you expecting? It's a dangerous place!"
	quest.5ED3D2D9B98D57A3.quest_desc: [
		"robots don't need to breathe"
		"(also oxygen mechanics are really not very fun at all)"
	]
	quest.6A607F1C57E734FE.quest_desc: ["You thought those bricks from before were good? You haven't seen anything yet!"]
	quest.72A041F528A47488.quest_desc: ["Nothing burns on Mars, so you'll have to get creative with how you heat things up..."]
	quest.75007C37FEBA9C7F.quest_desc: ["How good are you with saunas? How about being cooked alive? That's right! By melting yourself down, you can extract liquid soul essence from yourself, and you can use it to create a haunt furnace, capable of turning items into their hellish mirror images!"]
	quest.75007C37FEBA9C7F.quest_subtitle: "We're gonna need a bigger furnace...."
	quest.75007C37FEBA9C7F.title: "Selling Your Soul To The Devil"
	quest.78322A55CBC580FA.quest_desc: ["There are meteorites scattered all across the surface of the planet.... They contain some trace metals that'll be very useful!"]
	quest.7C3C7BC560340947.quest_desc: ["By infesting some conglomerate stone, you can make a strange, petrified mushroom rock capable of having plants root on it!"]
	task.071AB760C7DEB91B.title: "Welcome to The Wild Red Yonder!"
	task.12F254C45E48AC34.title: "Environmental Hazards"
	task.168E433B7F7F8179.title: "Oxygen"
	task.40BE194E4D3A6804.title: "Food: You Need It"
	task.4EDDC29A859A6F9B.title: "Any #botania:shimmering_mushrooms"
	task.4F587374B77B5DBC.title: "Akhashic Tome"
}
